  <body>
    <nav class="topbar">
      <button type="button" id="themeToggle">☾</button>
    </nav>
    <div class="layout">
      <nav class="sidebar">
        <input type="text" id="searchBar" placeholder="Search errors..." />
        <h2>List of Errors</h2>
        <ul id="errorList"></ul>
      </nav>
      <main class="main">
        <h1>Mod-Related Issues</h1>
        <h2>Briefing:</h2>
        <p>
          You experience framerate drops, freezing, crashes, or failure to
          launch the game after changing your mod files.
        </p>

        <h2>Likely Cause:</h2>
        <p>
          Incompatible, outdated, or performance-heavy mods are examples of
          possible culprits.
        </p>

        <h2>General Fixes (try in order):</h2>

        <h3>1. Remove all mods.</h3>
        <p>
          To verify whether mods are in fact the problem, remove all of them,
          and then test the game.
        </p>

        <p>To remove the modded files:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Open Steam. Navigate to "Library".</li>
          <li>Right click the game - Manage - Browse Local Files.</li>
          <li>
            Move the lua scripts, the "REFramework" folder, the "dinput8.dll"
            file, and any other content you recognize as modded
            <b>outside the "MonsterHunterWilds" folder</b> and into a backup folder
            to make restoration easy.
          </li>
          <li>
            Test the game. If the issue is gone, mods are likely to have been
            the cause.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2. Re-Add Mods One by One.</h3>
        <p>
          After confirming the game is stable without mods, you may begin adding
          them one by one, while
          <strong
            >testing the game for a session or two after every addition to
            isolate the culprit</strong
          >. <br /><br />Make sure that your modded files are downloaded from
          <strong
            >trusted sources such as Nexus Mods or known GitHub repositories and
            that they are all up-to-date.</strong
          >
          If you are uncertain of whether your mods are of the latest release, find
          their official release pages to verify you have the latest version.<br
          /><br />When adding modded files to your game's folder, be sure to
          <strong
            >follow the creator's instructions carefully regarding their
            placement in the game's folder.</strong
          >
        </p>

        <p>
          <b>If you find the culprit</b>, make sure it's updated. If it still
          causes instability, consider removing it and finding an alternative.
          You may research and verify from community reports whether the mod is
          troublesome for others or only your specific device. If the former, a
          message to the creator to raise awareness may be your only option if
          workarounds are not present.
        </p>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
